Kind: ablation
Issue: #723
Takes out: nothing -- a probe: thread_select() leaves first_quantum FALSE where it set it TRUE, so a thread with a peer of its priority waiting is handed over at the next tick instead of at the end of its quantum. preempt_test's three threads, bound to one processor, then change hands about once a tick, ten times what a quantum of min_quantum ticks promises. Before #723 the test counted nothing, and passed it.
Accel: tcg,kvm
Run: --entry 21 300 -smp 1
Expect: preempt_test: WRONG .* changed hands [0-9]+ times in [0-9]+ ticks
Note: entry 21 is -P with the HPET forced as the clock; at one processor the test is the form load_context() starts. 723-quantum-four-times asks the other side, at four processors on entry 5.

